      "gender": "male",
      "houseId": 75,
      "dateOfBirth": "1870",
      "dateOfDeath": "1940",
      "legitimacyStatus": "bastard",
      "notes": "Bastard son of an early Wilson lord's younger brother and a northern farmwoman. Even in exile, the Wilfrey blood ran hot. The Wilsons acknowledged Farren quietly — they had spent a century building legitimacy and a bastard was an inconvenience, not a scandal. He farmed near Grantholm his whole life."
    },

    {
      "_comment": "=== BASTARDS — DUM- PREFIX (MOTHER'S NAME, RARE) ===",
      "_tempId": "person_cerys_dumwilfrey",
