      "gender": "female",
      "houseId": 70,
      "dateOfBirth": "1890",
      "dateOfDeath": "1965",
      "legitimacyStatus": "bastard",
      "notes": "Born to a woman of House Wilfrey of Fourhearth and a common sailor. Her mother was a younger daughter with no marriage prospects — the sailor was a passing indiscretion. But the Wilfrey name was too valuable to abandon. Cerys bore it her whole life as a Dumwilfrey — not quite Wilfrey, but close enough to open some doors and close others. Lived in the harbour communities of Fourhearth."
    },
    {
      "_tempId": "person_annis_dumwilfrey",
      "firstName": "Annis",
      "lastName": "Dumwilfrey",
      "gender": "female",
      "houseId": 70,
      "dateOfBirth": "1945",
      "dateOfDeath": null,
      "legitimacyStatus": "bastard",
      "notes": "Born to a woman of House Wilfrey of Bramblehall and a travelling merchant. Dum-named bastards are rare — most children take their father's name. But in the Wilfrey context, the mother's name carries enough weight that some choose it deliberately. Annis grew up on the edges of Bramblehall's woodland communities, neither fully inside nor fully outside."
    }
